1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,930
Slide 32 diagrams THE DANGER OF SCREEN-CAPTURING LEAKS: The Accidental Ingestion Threat.

2
00:00:07,330 --> 00:00:11,897
This is the most common accidental data breach in companies today!

3
00:00:11,897 --> 00:00:15,150
Look at the 3-step disaster sequence on screen:

4
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:23,210
Step 1: An employee turns on a desktop vision AI assistant to help summarize a public tech article on their left monitor.

5
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:31,410
Step 2: An urgent HR message pops up on the right monitor showing employee salary spreadsheets or patient social security numbers!

6
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:41,290
And Step 3: The screen scraper takes a full desktop snapshot, inadvertently ingesting those private medical and salary pixels into the cloud prompt!

7
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:48,550
The employee didn't mean to leak data, but the unconstrained vision agent sent sensitive PII straight into the cloud pipeline!

8
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:54,730
That's why unconstrained full-screen capture is completely banned in our Spark OS architecture!

9
00:00:55,130 --> 00:01:02,280
Visual AI must be bounded by window-specific capture filters and real-time PII redaction shields.

